# GitHub Flow (repository policy)

- **Never integrate substantive work by pushing directly to `shared` `main`** when a PR is expected: use a **`feature/<short-description>`** branch from updated `main`.
- **Never commit on `main`**: if the working tree is dirty on `main`, immediately create a `feature/...` branch and commit there.
- **Commits:** **Atomic** — one logical change per commit (revert-friendly, review-friendly).
- **`main`:** Changes land **only through a pull request** with green CI ([`allium-specs`](../../.github/workflows/allium-specs.yml) job `check`).
- **Merge strategy:** Use **Squash and merge** or **Rebase and merge** only. **Do not** use “Create a merge commit” for PRs into `main` — keep **linear history** ([docs/guides/github-flow.md](../../docs/guides/github-flow.md)).
- **CLI:** Prefer **`gh`** for `gh pr create`, `gh pr checks`, `gh pr merge --squash` / `--rebase` ([install](https://cli.github.com/)). Use **`git`** for branching and commits.

Canonical guide: [docs/guides/github-flow.md](../../docs/guides/github-flow.md).
